        "payload": "tree d8367b6cf4792062f9124970b950ae555f3486f1\nparent d747d9c054a6fc9c77f3bb84a82e021475041e2b\nauthor DanConwayDev <DanConwayDev@protonmail.com> 1778928681 +0000\ncommitter DanConwayDev <DanConwayDev@protonmail.com> 1778928681 +0000\n\nfix: preserve original merge-base on ff push to PR branch\n\nWhen fast-forward pushing new commits onto a pr/ branch that is backed\nby an existing PR event (kind 1618), the generated PR update event\nincorrectly set the merge-base tag to the parent of the first *new*\ncommit — i.e. the previous PR tip — rather than the original branch\ndivergence point.\n\nThe fix reads the merge-base tag from the root PR event and forwards it\nunchanged into the PR update event, falling back to\nget_commit_parent(first_commit) only when no merge-base tag is present\n(e.g. older PR events that predate the tag).\n",
