        "payload": "tree 008d41f9655f6cc28d3c25c2270e2ceb913e162c\nparent 7a42ea6a053d2e462f8a1f4b681a36ba25f7e417\nauthor DanConwayDev <DanConwayDev@protonmail.com> 1778775338 +0000\ncommitter DanConwayDev <DanConwayDev@protonmail.com> 1778925920 +0000\n\nfeat: force PR mode when commits contain submodule entries\n\nPatches touching submodule entries (mode 160000) crash libgit2 on the\nreceiving end (SIGSEGV in apply_to_tree).  Rather than waiting for the\ncrash to happen during apply, detect the condition up-front in `ngit send`\nand route the proposal as a PR so the commits are pushed directly instead\nof being sent as patch events.\n\nAdds `do_commits_contain_submodules` to the `RepoActions` trait (reusing\n`make_patch_from_commit` + the same mode-160000 heuristic already used in\n`create_commit_from_patch`) and ORs it into the `should_be_pr` decision\nalongside the existing size check.\n",
